# The play camera's run (F5, docs/design/camera.md): through a door, under
# a tree's crown, up stairs and along a cliff's edge, with the camera at its
# default 9 m. Every frame's camera is logged; `camera check` fails on a pop
# (a frame that moved it faster than the limit) or an eye in a wall.
# Run by tools/drive/camera.sh on a fresh world whose operator is this
# character (`yard` builds the course round it).

yard
camera record
wait 1

# --- 1. through the house: in at its south door, out at its north door ------
walk-path 1 -4 1 -12 1 -19
# --- 2. under the tree's crown, past its trunk ------------------------------
walk-path 1 -24 0 -29
# --- 3. up the stairs onto the cliff ----------------------------------------
walk-path 1 -31 1 -40
# --- 4. along the cliff's east edge -----------------------------------------
walk-path 2.5 -42 3.2 -45 3.2 -57
wait 0.5
# --- 5. the camera swung out over the edge and back, looking up and down ----
swing 100 20
wait 0.5
swing -200 -10
wait 0.5
swing 100 -10
# --- 6. back along the edge, down the stairs, back through the door ---------
walk-path 0 -55 1 -41 1 -31 1 -20 1 -12 1 -2
shot camera-end
# --- 7. along the house's east wall, a shoulder's width from it -------------
walk-path 6.6 -5 6.6 -13
wait 1

camera check 60

# --- 8. (set-up) back to the wall: the camera is squeezed to the head and
# the character fades out of its way
turn -90
wait 1
shot camera-fade
